  "worked_solution": "First, we find ${f}^{\u2032}(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(t) & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}\u20612t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((t+2)^{2})\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8-2\\operatorname{sin}\u20612t,\\,\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}},\\,2(t+2)\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute ${f}^{\u2032}(\\pi )$ we substitute $t=\\pi $ into the expression for ${f}^{\u2032}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(\\pi ) & =\u27e8-2\\operatorname{sin}\u20612\\pi ,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2(\\pi +2)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e80,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2(\\pi +2)\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
